<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF wins Spanish army contract.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF wins Spanish army contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French defence electronics company Thomson-CSF said on Friday its Thomson-CSF Communications unit and its Spanish partner Amper Programas had won contracts worth about 600 million francs to supply a tactical digital radio system for the Spanish army.  </p>
<p>Amper Programas is a joint ventre between Thomson-CSF and the Amper group.</p>
<p>Thomson-CSF is supplying a network switching subsystem based its modular tactical switch, which serves similar radios used by the French and U.S. forces.</p>
<p>It will transfer technology to Amper to build the command subsystem and which will allow it to develop future systems and support the network.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
